  "notes": "The six product states phi^5 over the single-qubit stabilizer states are independent in the six-dimensional symmetric subspace (in the Hamming-weight basis they are e_0, e_5, and the Vandermonde rows (z^w)_w for z = 1, -1, i, -i), so they span Sym^5 and every symmetric five-qubit state, |sqrtT>^5 among them, has chi <= 6; this is the generic value chi_5 = 6 of Lovitz and Steffan (arXiv:2110.07781, Section 1.3). With qubit_sqrtT-m5-lower-6.json (exact census through the Galois-forced subspace) the cell is exact, chi(|sqrtT>^5) = 6, gamma log_2(6)/5 = 0.5170 against the published 1/2. The construction stops here: at six qubits the six product states span only the hyperplane f(1) = f(5) of Sym^6, and every symmetric six-qubit stabilizer state has equal amplitudes on weights 1 and 5, so Sym^6 is not spanned by symmetric stabilizer states and a seven-term decomposition of |sqrtT>^6, which would beat 1/2, needs non-symmetric terms."
